    "input": {
      "body": "Hi Matt,\n\nMy last note asked about recurring document bottlenecks at Alipour Law Group. I wrote a short article on why removing one bottleneck can still leave the wider process unchanged.\n\nGetting value from AI often means changing how preparation, review, and follow-up fit together. That's shaping how we work with PI firms at Possible Minds.\n\nhttps://getpossibleminds.com/t/oSEIuiV2nA\n\nAs the firm's founder, which seems harder to change: the software or the routines around it? I'd value even a one-line reply.\n\nBest,\nPranav\nFounder, Possible Minds",
      "subject": "Re: where AI could compound at Alipour Law Group",
